        "original_id": "f13140e5-1ea2-55b9-bab9-a931500e9804",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Melville Arthur \"Sparky\" Vail\n- Organizations: New York Rangers, National Hockey League\n- Places: Meaford, Ontario, New York metropolitan area\n- Topics: ice hockey, NHL franchise history\n\nFacts:\n- The New York Rangers joined the National Hockey League in 1926 as an expansion franchise.\n- Melville Arthur \"Sparky\" Vail was born on July 5, 1906 in Meaford, Ontario.\n- Melville Arthur \"Sparky\" Vail was a professional ice hockey player in the National Hockey League for the New York Rangers.\n- Melville Arthur \"Sparky\" Vail played 50 games for the New York Rangers over the 1928–29 and 1929–30 seasons, scoring four goals and five points.\n- The New York Rangers are one of three National Hockey League franchises in the New York metropolitan area, along with the New Jersey Devils and New York Islanders.\n- Melville Arthur \"Sparky\" Vail died on January 29, 1983.",
